# Dev vs production branches

- **`dev`** — local development. Commit feature work here. Deploy locally with `scripts/deploy-local.ps1` (Windows) or `scripts/deploy-local.sh`.
- **`main`** — production only. Merging to `main` triggers GitHub Actions deploy to https://indukuru.online.

## When implementing features

1. Work on `dev` (create/checkout if missing).
2. After changes, run local deploy script so the user can test at http://localhost:8080.
3. Do **not** push to `main` until the user confirms local testing passed.
4. When the user approves, merge `dev` → `main` and push `main`.

## Do not

- Push untested feature commits directly to `main`.
- Run production GCP deploy scripts for local testing — use Docker Compose instead.

See `LOCAL_DEV.md` for full workflow.
